    "details": "The Erlang/OTP project reports:\n\n> OTP 29.1.1, 28.5.0.7 and 27.3.4.18 fix the following issues:\n>\n> - CVE-2026-89422: TLS 1.3 client skips server authentication on\n>   unsolicited PSK. A pre_shared_key extension in the ServerHello that\n>   the client never offered causes the client to complete the handshake\n>   without validating the server\\'s certificate.\n> - CVE-2026-68956: SSH session channel exhaustion. The max_channels\n>   daemon option only limited channels with an active handler, so an\n>   authenticated client could open unlimited idle session channels and\n>   exhaust the memory of the whole Erlang VM.\n> - CVE-2026-65634: Superlinear CPU denial-of-service in the asn1 OID\n>   decoder via large base-128 arcs.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0473",
